-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

rlpr 1.41 is now available.  this release largely contains fixes for
BSD-isms that some berkeley lpd's count on.  you are encouraged to
upgrade if you were having problems getting rlpr to work properly with
your lpd (especially with regard to burst pages).

If you weren't having any problems, there's no real need to upgrade --
however, if the holiday spirit has got you in that upgrade mood, go
right ahead.

Briefly, rlpr uses TCP/IP to send print jobs to lpd servers anywhere on
a network.  Unlike lpr, it *does not* require that the remote printers
be explicitly known to the machine you wish to print from, (e.g. through
/etc/printcap) and thus is considerably more flexible and requires less
administration.

Most importantly, one can use rlpr to print from a machine one does not
have root access on to a machine one does.  (no, this isn't a security
hole).  There are also some additinal configurations which are possible.
Please read rlpr's README for details.

rlpr can be obtained from the following sources:

    Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/system/Printing
                    65kB rlpr-1.41.tar.gz
    Alternate-site: sherilyn.wustl.edu /pub/

have fun and hope to see you at uselinux,
meem

