Title:		dmsdosfs
Version:	0.7.5
Entered-date:	21DEC96
Description:	dmsdos filesystem for Linux: extends msdos filesystem to allow
                full read and restricted write access to msdos/win95 compressed
                partitions (msdos files like dblspace.xxx and drvspace.xxx and
                stacvol.xxx). The following configurations are supported:
                 - DoubleSpace / DriveSpace compressed msdos 6.x partitions
                   (read-write, fully supported),
                 - DoubleSpace / DriveSpace compressed win95 partitions
                   (read-write, fully supported),
                 - DriveSpace 3 (from Plus! pack) compressed win95 partitions
                   (read-write, without Ultra compression method support),
                 - Stacker 3 compressed partitions (read-write, but write
                   access currently without compression),
                 - Stacker 4 compressed partitions (read-write, compression
                   currently experimental)
                *** It does NOT support new FAT32 filesystems. ***
                This version is compatible with the 1.2.13, most 1.3.xx,
                pre-2.0.x and the 2.0.x kernels. Experimental support for
                2.1.x kernels has been added, but it may not work with brand
                new kernels. Dmsdos can run together with vfat
                or umsdos and can handle win95 long filenames itself. This
                version includes the dmsdos daemon for fast write access.
                Support for Linux < 2.0.1 is likely to disappear soon.
