An astute reader pointed out to me that my previous announcement failed
to describe what the HFS filesystem actually IS.  So let me try again...

New official and test releases of hfs_fs, the HFS filesystem module for
Linux are now available from http://www-sccm.Stanford.EDU/~hargrove/HFS/

This kernel loadable module implements the Macintosh's Hierarchical File
System (HFS), which has been the native filesystem of the Apple Macintosh
line since the Mac Plus.

The official release is also in ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/
to be moved to ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/ALPHA/hfs/

The new official release, hfs_fs-0.7.7, fixes two serious bugs that were
present in previous versions.  So, I strongly recommend the upgrade to
all hfs_fs users.  Version 0.7.7 compiles with Linux kernel version 2.0.1
through at least 2.1.14.

The new test release, hfs_fs-pre-0.8-3, differs from pre-0.8-2 mainly in
that it fixes the same bugs fixed in 0.7.7 and will compile with later
2.1.x kernels.

