Linux activity in Hungary
=========================

It is all started in November 1995 with the launch of the Mailing List of
the Hungarian Linux Users. At that time only a few Hungrians (mainly
students from several technical universities) had any idea about what is
Linux is.

The mailing list begun to grow, more and more people joind to it. In May
1996 the members of the list decided to have a personal meeting. In the
city of Debrecen 25 linuxers gathered togheter for the very first time
where they have succesfuly installed the first ever working SPARC Linux in
Hungary.

The summer was generaly quiet. In September some of the list memebers
decided to start a seperate list for the beginners, where their questions
are answered in details. 30th of November was an other good time to meet:
but this time more then two hundred linuxers were present.

In December the Home Page of the Hungarian Linux Users has won the
so-called "Rulez-prize" of the "Internetto" on-line magazine and was
presented in the Hungarian state television as well. This homepage is
mirrored on several servers accros the country.

Hungarians are involved in several projects and there are also traces of
us in the kernel source and distribution. Hungarian commercial companies
and Internet providers are now aware of the power of Linux and slowly it
is recognized as a real operating system, as a real alternative. The Linux
distributions and applications are presented on one of the Hungarian
computer magazine's CD month-by-month and the Hungarian translations of
HOWTOs and FAQs and all sorts of documents are in progress as well. The
first Hungarian language book about Linux was published recently and there
is much more to come...

For more information about Hungarians in Linux check out
http://www.datanet.hu/generations/linux/enghupride.html
or if you speak Hungarian, go and visit the "award-winning" ;-)
http://www.cab.u-szeged.hu/local/linux

Later,
Tamas
(defiant)

