-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

With the latest update (961211) MkLinux for Power Macintosh now supports
PCI bus Power Macintosh systems.

PCI support has been tested on Power Macintosh 7200, 7500, 8500 and 9500's.
It has not been tested on 7600's, 8200s or PCI clones. However, there is a
very good chance these machines will work with this release. If you have a
7600, an 8200 and/or PCI clone and install this release, please let us know
if this works or not. You can send mail to bugs@mklinux.apple.com.

Support is still incomplete for the 7200 (cosmetic bugs) and 9500 (no X11
support for the ATI video card). Your mileage may vary!  We're sorry, but
support is not available for Performas or Powerbooks at this time.

Note that the MkLinux DR2 distribution is required to install PCI support.
PCI support will not work with a MkLinux DR1 system.

The PCI installation kit is available for anonymous download from
ftp://ftp.mklinux.apple.com/pub/MkLinux_DR2/PCI. More information is
available from our Web pages
<URL:http://www.mklinux.apple.com/DR2/updates/961211.html>.

Vicki Brown
Apple Computer Leveraged Technologies Group
MkLinux project

