-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hi Unix-Gamers!

As XBlast is now going it fourth year (the first release was in November
1993), I want to announce a new release, XBlast 2.2.  It features
optional sound support for Linux, which is available in a separate
file. It is available via anonymous ftp from the following ftp-servers:

ftp.x.org:       /contrib/games/multiplayer/xblast-2.2.tar.gz
ftp.x.org:       /contrib/games/multiplayer/xblast-2.2-sound.tar.gz
sunsite.unc.edu: /pub/Linux/games/X11/video/xblast-2.2.tar.gz
sunsite.unc.edu: /pub/Linux/games/X11/video/xblast-2.2-sound.tar.gz

WHAT IS XBLAST?

XBlast is a multi-player arcade game for X11R5/R6. The game can be
played with at least two players and up to four players. It can use one
to four X displays for output. XBlast supports color and monochrome
graphics. It was inspired by the video/computer game Bomberman
(Dynablaster), which was to my knowledge first programmed for NEC's PC
Engine/Turbo Grafx. Other (commercial) versions of the original game
exist for IBM-PC, Atari ST, Amiga, NES, GameBoy and Super NES.

PLATFORMS

It should compile on almost any UN*X with X11R5/R6.  XBlast 2.0 was
tested under Linux, HPUX, Ultrix, SunOS, Solaris, NetBSD and IRIX.
Older version were known to run under OSF, AIX, LynxOS.

WHATS NEW IN V2.2

 o Support for up to 6 players

 o Team mode with 2 or 3 teams of two.

 o Sound support for Linux (in a separate archive).

 o tkXBlast - a vastly improved tcl/tk based XBlast launcher, featuring
   resource setup and game statistics.

 o 7 new levels

 o Keyboard customisation via X-Resources.

 o Short delay and bell when the restarts game after a pause.

 o Code optimisation for smoother game play for up to six players


Have fun blasting,

	Oliver Vogel

