-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hi all,

I would like to announce the universal mime plug-in for Netscape.
Basically, I was getting tired of not being able to listen to embedded
midi and wav music so I wrote this program.  It reads the mime type and
a associated application from a configuration file.  It then registers
the extension with Netscape so whenever a web page with a embedded file
is downloaded, the plugin will be called.  While it was designed for
audio, it can easily handle any other embedded mime type.

Note that in order to list to midi or wave music, you need applications
like playmidi or wavplay.  It also does not support streaming nor the
audio controls found in the Windows versions of Netscape.

I hope that this may be of use to you.

LSM entry:

Begin
Title:          Universal Mime Plug-in for Netscape
Version:        1.0
Entered-date:   December 15, 1996
Description:    This is a Universal (I hope) mime plug-in for Linux.
Basically, given a configuration file, it registers the plug-in with a
corresponding mime type.  For each mime type, there must be an
associated extension and application to run.  For instance, given the
mime type audio/x-midi, it would register with Netscape that it can
handle embedded files with the .mid extensions.  Of course, a program
like playmidi is required to play the file.  Take a look at the sample
configuration file for examples of how to configure the plug-in.

This program was developed to play embedded midi and wav music.  Since
it requires separate programs to actually play the file, it does not
support streaming.  Nor does it have the funky midi and wav controls
seen in the Windows version of Netscape, although I would like to add
them eventually.

