 Visual Tcl 1.01b
 December 5, 1996

 Announcing the first beta release of Visual Tcl, a freely-available, high-
 quality application development environment for UNIX, Windows and Macintosh
 platforms. Visual Tcl is written entirely in Tcl/Tk and covered by the GNU
 General Public License.

 I started Visual Tcl in late 1995 as a tool for prototyping Unix GUIs for
 systems management tools. Since then a lot of features have been added which
 make it more complete as application development environment.

 Some of the features:

 o Written entirely in Tcl. No custom libraries.
 o Extensible to add new geometry managers and widgets.
 o GUI interface for most aspects of Tk development.
    o function and variable browsers
    o attribute manager
    o bind editor
    o menu editor
 o Supports Pack, Place and Grid geometry managers.
 o Imports existing Tcl code.
 o Distinct Run and Edit modes (like Visual Basic).
 o More intuitive GUI development than XF or GuiBuilder.

 There are a lot of things I'd like to clean up or extend (such as a
 widget tree browser), but it's time to seek external feedback and testing.

 Check it out:

   http://www.neuron.com/stewart/vtcl

- -- 
