EXT2-OS2 VERSION 2.10 (32 BITS EDITION)

WHAT IS EXT2-OS2?

ext2-os2.ifs is a file system driver that allows OS/2 to seamlessly
access Linux native partitions (ext2fs partitions) in both read and
write modes.  Once installed, Linux partitions appear as standard OS/2
drive letters, one per Linux partition. It is a port of the original
Linux ext2fs kernel code.

ext2-os2 can even be used without Linux, as it can format or check ext2
file systems directly from OS/2. This can be useful for people who need
huge cache sizes, for large compilations for instance.

MAIN NEW FEATURES SINCE V2.0

 - Added support for e2fsck and mke2fs. Booting Linux is no longer required to
   format or check an ext2 file system ; this can now be done from OS/2.
 - Improved performance.
 - Included boot capabilities present in the 16 bits version : this version
   can boot OS/2 from a Linux partition.

WHERE TO FIND EXT2-OS2

You can find ext2-os2 mainly on the following sites (or in their
incoming directory):

  ftp://ftp-os2.nmsu.edu/os2/diskutil/ext2_210.zip (or /incoming)

  ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/Filesystems/ext2/ext2_210.zip
  (or /pub/Linux/Incoming)

  ftp://ftp-os2.cdrom.com/pub/os2/diskutil/ext2_210.zip (or /pub/os2/incoming)

DISCLAIMER

I'm developing this driver during my spare time.  Even if I work for
IBM, IBM isn't implied in any way with this driver, I develop it at
home.

FEEDBACK AND SUPPORT

Please feel free to contact me for any question on ext2-os2. You are
also encouraged to give me some feedback on how it works on your system
and what new features you would like ... this helps me improve it ! Both
success stories and disasters interest me.

- -- 
