 This is to announce the availability of version 0.3 (ALPHA) of the DIPC
package. DIPC stands for Distributed Inter-Process Communication. It
could be used to build and program multi-computers and distributed
systems out of ordinary Intel-based PCs, connected over a TCP/IP
network. DIPC works by making UNIX System V IPC mecahnisms (shared
memories, semaphores and messages) function transparently in a network.

 The files dipc-0.3.tgz and dipc-0.3.lsm can be obtained by anonymous
ftp from sunsite.unc.edu, in directory /pub/Linux/Incoming, or
/pub/Linux/ALPHA.

 This version replaces DIPC v0.15 and v0.15pl1. All previuos versions
are hereby declared obsolete.

 The main feature of this version is the ability of DIPC to use 4KB
pages or whole segments for its Distributed Shared Memory (DSM)
management. It is possible to configure some computers to use pages, and
others to use segments, and THEY CAN WORK WITH EACH OTHER. See the files
in the package to know about other changes in DIPC v0.3.

 I am also seeking volunteers to setup a web page and/or a mailing list
for DIPC. What is needed is the necessary computer resources AND some
experience with WWW and mailing lists, as I lack both.

