Dear all,

This is to announce the general availability, free of charge, of the
IBM Webbin' CMIP Technology Release 3.  Webbin' CMIP is a research
project at IBM Zurich Research Laboratory aimed to simplify the access
to network management information and resources.  The core part of
Webbin' is a component-based application named Liaison.  Liaison
allows people to manage CMIP and SNMP network resources using a
conventional Web-browser.  If your browser supports VRML (Virtual
Reality Modeling Language) you can also visualise 3D network
topologies.  Additionally Liaison comes with Java/C++ external
bindings which allow people to write simple applications and applets
for the purpose of network management.

Liaison is available for AIX, MacOS, Linux and Win95/NT and it can be
freely downloaded from:
       http://misa.zurich.ibm.com/Webbin/ (final '/' please).

Note:
1. This release will expire at the end of June 1997.
2. CMIP is supported only by the AIX personality.
3. DO NOT register if you're a Webbin registered user.

Several papers and a new Internet Draft which relate to Webbin have
been added to the Web site. Feel free to download them.

Do not forget to send me your feedbacks and error reports, if any.

Please read the license before to download the software.

Best regards,

						Luca Deri

